\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Population pretraining objective}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{pretraining}
\tag{loss}

\p{The \newvocab{population pretraining objective} associated with
#{\mathcal D_{\rm pre}} is
##{
L_{\rm pre}(\theta)
=\mathbb E_{X\sim\mathcal D_{\rm pre}}[\ell(\theta;X)],
}
provided the expectation exists.}

\p{The language-model loss used in
\citet{sec. 2.2}{kaplan2020scaling} is an average next-token loss over the
chosen data distribution. The population form separates that target quantity
from a finite corpus and from the random minibatches used by an optimizer.}
